        "text": "# OR (`||`)\n\n**OR (`||`)** is a logical operator used in conditional statements. \n\nFor a condition using **OR** to be true, **at least one** part of the condition must be true. \n\n| A | B | A &#124;&#124; B |\n|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| T | T | T |\n| T | F | T |\n| F | T | T |\n| F | F | F |\n\n\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/325240ce958c0eb5bdae2a7dc87c3287-OR1.png",
        "key": "undefined-ea03636a-a1b5-4568-be2b-86c3c6462665",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      }
    ]
